      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] ✅ **Approved** — All checks pass. [🔗](http://go/tj/cns/gg-d/home/tomhughes@google.com/review_trajectories/cl8281008_40647a3b-4643-4142-a1d0-64f84be98665.pb)\n\n### Review Summary\n*   **Functionality:** The logic correctly wraps the OTP key programming loop with `irq_lock()` and `irq_unlock()` to prevent interruptions. The assertion accurately verifies that interrupts are disabled before writing.\n*   **Architecture \u0026 Component Fit:** The logic fits cleanly into the OTP driver and the assertions are correctly placed in the write functions.\n*   **Code Simplicity:** The changes are simple, minimalistic, and use standard `irq_lock`/`irq_unlock` idioms without adding unnecessary state.\n*   **Idiomaticity \u0026 Readability:** The use of `ASSERT(!is_interrupt_enabled());` inside the hardware layer and mock is the idiomatic way to verify execution context in this codebase.\n*   **Security:** Disabling interrupts during security-critical operations like OTP key programming correctly prevents side-channel interruptions or partial writes.\n*   **Testing:** Test coverage is good. It verifies that interrupts are locked inside the mock and properly restored in `test_otp_key`.\n*   **CL Size \u0026 Scope:** Size: S (+23, -1). The CL is atomic and focuses on a single logical change.\n*   **Commit Message:** The commit message clearly explains the \"Why\" and \"What\" of the changes, and includes correct Chromium OS formatting.",
